# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AUTHORITATIVE source of HTTP security headers for app.seqrets.app.
#
# app.seqrets.app is hosted on Cloudflare Pages (project "seqrets-app"),
# deployed by direct upload of the static export from
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml. Next.js copies this file into out/, and
# Cloudflare Pages applies it natively. Editing this file and deploying IS
# how headers change. Don't also set them in a Cloudflare Transform Rule for
# this host: a rule silently overrides this file and the two will drift.
#
# The CSP is duplicated as a <meta http-equiv> tag in src/app/layout.tsx
# (defense-in-depth in case the host ever stops sending headers).
# Keep the two in sync. The one intended difference: frame-ancestors appears
# ONLY here, because browsers ignore it inside a <meta> CSP. Any new outbound
# fetch origin must be added to connect-src in BOTH places.
#
# HSTS deliberately omits "preload". Don't add it without an explicit decision.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  X-Permitted-Cross-Domain-Policies: none
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src 'self' https://api.coinbase.com https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
